      "text": "1. To find the probability that exactly two of the dice show an even number, we first need to find the probability of exactly one of the dice showing an even number.\n\n2. The probability that exactly one die shows an even number is P(both others show odd number).\n\n3. Let's calculate the desired probability:\n\n   P(both others show odd number) = P(6 faces show odd number) * P(6 faces show odd number)\n                                     = ${11 \\choose 3}{12 \\choose 1}{12 \\choose 1}$\n                                     = 46,259\n\n4. To find the probability of a fair 12-sided die showing an even number, we divide the number of even faces (6) by the number of faces (12):\n\n   $P(\\text{even number}) = \\frac{11}{12}$\n\n5. Now, to find the probability of a fair 12-sided die showing an odd number, we have:\n\n   $P(\\text{odd number}) = \\frac{1}{12}$\n\n6. We multiply these probabilities:\n\n   $P(\\text{exactly one die shows even number}) = P(both others show odd number) * P(\\text{even number})$ * $P(\\text{odd number})$\n                                    = $\\frac{46,259}{1,035,510}$\n                                    = 0.00449\n\nHence, the final answer is $\\boxed{0.00449}$.",
